# Build-context filter for the Rust worker images.
#
# This file MUST live at the workspace root and MUST be named `.dockerignore`.
# The SDK uses the ignore list twice, through two different code paths:
#
# - uploading the build context, which reads whatever path the image's
#   DockerIgnore layer points at (any filename works); and
# - computing the image tag (`Image._get_hash_digest`), which builds a
#   `DockerfileIgnore(<dir of that path>)` — and that class only ever loads
#   `<dir>/.dockerignore`, and only matches paths *underneath* `<dir>`.
#
# So an ignore file with any other name, or sitting anywhere but an ancestor of
# the copied sources, is silently a no-op for the tag hash: the hash then walks
# and reads every ignored file, and every launcher edit mints a new tag and
# rebuilds the image.
#
# NOTE: supplying a .dockerignore REPLACES the SDK's standard ignore patterns,
# so everything to exclude must be listed here.
target
**/target
.git
**/.git
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
# The worker image builds Rust only; excluding Python and docs keeps launcher and
# README edits from invalidating the image tag. Both forms: a bare pattern matches
# only the context root, as with `target` / `**/target` above.
#
# Markdown is safe to drop only because no crate embeds one at build time (no
# `include_str!("../README.md")` anywhere). Add an exception here if that changes.
*.py
**/*.py
*.md
**/*.md
.venv
**/.venv
.flyte
**/.flyte
.DS_Store
